From: <author>
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86/intel/pmc: Don't truncate hardware sleep time to 32 bits

pmc_core_is_s0ix_failed() reports the time spent in hardware sleep with

	pm_report_hw_sleep_time((u32)(s0ix_counter - pmcdev->s0ix_counter));

Both counter values are already scaled to microseconds by
pmc_core_adjust_slp_s0_step(), so the u32 cast does not deal with a wrap
of the 32-bit SLP_S0 residency register. Instead it truncates the result
modulo 2^32 us, which is 71.6 minutes. Any s2idle period longer than that
is under-reported in /sys/power/suspend_stats/last_hw_sleep and
total_hw_sleep, while max_hw_sleep (set by the same driver) correctly
advertises the full counter range of about 145 hours.

Seen on a Meteor Lake-H laptop (ASUS GU605MI) after a 9331 s s2idle
period that spent 9322.6 s in S0i2.1 according to the PMC substate
residency counters:

	last_hw_sleep:  732664908	(= 9322.6 s - 2 * 4294.967296 s)
	max_hw_sleep:   523986009990

User space that divides last_hw_sleep by the suspend time to judge
whether s2idle worked reports a healthy night as "8% in S0ix".

Compute the difference in the scaled domain and add one full counter
period when the hardware counter wrapped.

Fixes: ddd66d634735 ("platform/x86/intel/pmc: core: Report duration of time in HW sleep state")
Reported-by: <reporter>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/intel/pmc/core.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/intel/pmc/core.c
@@ -2051,12 +2051,26 @@
 
 static inline bool pmc_core_is_s0ix_failed(struct pmc_dev *pmcdev)
 {
-	u64 s0ix_counter;
+	struct pmc *pmc = pmcdev->pmcs[PMC_IDX_MAIN];
+	u64 s0ix_counter, hw_sleep;
 
-	if (pmc_core_dev_state_get(pmcdev->pmcs[PMC_IDX_MAIN], &s0ix_counter))
+	if (pmc_core_dev_state_get(pmc, &s0ix_counter))
 		return false;
 
-	pm_report_hw_sleep_time((u32)(s0ix_counter - pmcdev->s0ix_counter));
+	/*
+	 * Both readings are already scaled to microseconds, so truncating the
+	 * difference to u32 does not handle a wrap of the 32-bit hardware
+	 * counter: it cuts every s2idle period longer than ~71.6 minutes
+	 * down modulo 2^32 us. Handle the wrap in the scaled domain instead.
+	 */
+	if (s0ix_counter >= pmcdev->s0ix_counter)
+		hw_sleep = s0ix_counter - pmcdev->s0ix_counter;
+	else
+		hw_sleep = s0ix_counter - pmcdev->s0ix_counter +
+			   pmc_core_adjust_slp_s0_step(pmc, U32_MAX) +
+			   pmc_core_adjust_slp_s0_step(pmc, 1);
+
+	pm_report_hw_sleep_time(hw_sleep);
 
 	if (s0ix_counter == pmcdev->s0ix_counter)
 		return true;
